{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393128-on-mantles-what-the-heck","id":1393128,"title":"On Mantles - What the Heck!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-31T10:02:42-07:00","id":1393128,"title":"On Mantles - What the Heck!?","content":"I'm having trouble wrapping my head around Mantles, and if someone can help me understand them, I'd appreciate it.<br /> <br /> Here's what I think I know:<br /> <br /> 1. Mantles are like a sort of divine alternate identity, a costume or overlay that adds and/or suppresses attributes and characteristics to a God's nature (the 'raging brute Ares' vs. 'consummate soldier Mars' dichotomy)<br /> <br /> 2. Mantles are accumulations of characteristics associated with Deeds, which collect to form the godly persona.<br /> <br /> 3. Gods are punished by Fate for acting too far outside certain Fatebound behaviors, which is why Mantles are so useful; they allow for a wider range of activities with a smaller range of negative consequences.<br /> <br /> Now here's what I theorize, but have no proof for:<br /> <br /> A. Gods can create new Mantles through the performance of Deeds and accumulation of Legend while divested of any pre-existing Mantles and Legend, taking on a period of relative weakness and vulnerability in hopes of investing in future capabilities.<br /> <br /> This about sums up the total of my understanding of Mantles. Can anyone see if I've messed up somewhere or made any errors in logic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:40:45-07:00","id":1393217,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s close to what I understand too.<br /> <br /> I would say a god can create a Mantle while keeping Legend, as long it\u2019s not on a god level (just need to be a demigod).<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think we will have any rules about Mantles until Gods (and the devs are far from having any kind idea of the rules expected to be used, as they are focused on Demigod now, that is already a pretty big thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-31-2020, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T17:59:24-07:00","id":1393272,"title":"","content":"Mantles are a vague concept as of yet. I think of them as a kind of Mythic Identity. I prefer to use them for instances of like, regional variations. When you have one culture that worships Zeus THIS way, but another that worships him THAT way, and the two are different aspects, that may be something akin to a Mantle.<br /> <br /> Until then I like to think of acts of Claiming Mantles and Mantles worn by different beings... Y'know, it's like recurring roles in a stage play. (Simile stolen from someone else, just an FYI)<br /> <br /> Like, okay, Hamlet. Hamlet is a play that's been performed countless times, by countless different actors playing AS Hamlet himself. And in this case, most of those actors both stick to the basic idea of who Hamlet is, but they also can play a little with the details to emphasize THIS trait or focus on THAT one. So they're different spins, and people can talk about their favorite... But they're all Hamlet.<br /> <br /> As Mateus noted, though, we don't have mechanics for Mantles, and we probably won't until the God book, with maybe some mentions about them in the Demigod book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T18:57:50-07:00","id":1393288,"title":"","content":"We get a few new 'Gods in an Alternate Mantle' in the Scion Companion that they just released to Kickstarter backers. A few Orisha becoming Loa, and the one that mentions the 'Mantle' changes the most Goibnui of the Tuatha being Gobannos of the Nementondevos (and also his time as Gofannon of the Welsh Pantheon). It sounds in the writing that he loses some Legend when the Nementondevos are destroyed, travels to the Welsh, re-becomes God Legend Level, they get destroyed and he moves to the Tuatha and repeats the process. It says that because his primary role is 'The Smith' and every Pantheon can use a 'Smith', his changing of Mantles was easy. There is definitely a few changes between his Nementondevos Mantle and his Tuatha Mantle, but the core identity is the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:21:34-07:00","id":1393316,"title":"","content":"Right. What we <i>don't</i> have are the mechanics of how you create or acquire one. I'm guessing that the way you create one is to live in the World and perform the appropriate Deeds to define one \u2014 something every Scion does naturally as they progress from Hero to God. But what about a second one?<br /> <br /> Ares developed his Legend as a brutish thug, and so the Mantle of Ares developed around that identity. But over time, the God behind the Ares Mantle matured and settled down into a much more responsible figure, and the Mantle of Ares started to constrain him too much. So he did whatever gods do to craft new Mantles, and forged the Mantle of Mars to reflect his new identity. <br /> <br /> It may be that the process of creating a new Mantle for yourself is intrinsically linked to creating a new Pantheon, or at least a sub-Pantheon: thus, Ares was able to craft the Mantle of Mars when the Theoi established the Roman sub-Pantheon; and a number of Orisha established new Mantles when they helps establish the new Loa sub-Pantheon. And so on. <br /> <br /> But yeah; for now, this is all just speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T01:43:03-07:00","id":1393376,"title":"","content":"I mean, I think at Hero level, the closest you have to a Mantle is found in your Legendary Titles. A collection of your Titles and your Deeds and your Callings. It's the beginning of forming an Identity.<br /> <br /> I figure the mechanics of building a Mantle is accomplishing Deeds. Doing stuff.<br /> <br /> We Know who Zeus is. We Know what he does. The big Law Thunder Sky fellow who cut his siblings from the stomach of his father, who led the charge against Typhon. Whose very presence ensures Law, especially Xenia, the Law of Hospitality. The answers to &quot;Who is Zeus?&quot; is the Mantle.<br /> <br /> I look forward to seeing how Mantles may address regional variations of Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:26:36-07:00","id":1393418,"title":"","content":"I hope there's at least one god who develops mantles by absorbing his Scions as they reach apotheosis. Wouldn't that be a kick in the shorts? You, as a Scion, perform all these mythic deeds, and then, as you're about to become a god, your parent swoops in and assumes your identity, leaving you with nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:35:55-07:00","id":1393421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393128-on-mantles-what-the-heck?p=1393418#post1393418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope there's at least one god who develops mantles by absorbing his Scions as they reach apotheosis. Wouldn't that be a kick in the shorts? You, as a Scion, perform all these mythic deeds, and then, as you're about to become a god, your parent swoops in and assumes your identity, leaving you with nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you take account of the several incarnations of the Devas, that\u2019s basically what they do. They don\u2019t leave the Scion with nothing, they leave nothing of the Scion at all as the Scion becomes part of the original god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:51:30-07:00","id":1393425,"title":"","content":"That's not what I want to see, though. I want to see something predatory which leaves a victim behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:56:55-07:00","id":1393428,"title":"","content":"There really aren't any Gods that assholish in the core books, or mostly in general... despite what DnD et all like to throw about, 'Evil' Gods aren't really a thing, and that idea is slipping into 1e Aztec territory, and while you can do that in your games, it's going counter to the respectful tone 2e has generally been trying to set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:59:58-07:00","id":1393429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393128-on-mantles-what-the-heck?p=1393421#post1393421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you take account of the several incarnations of the Devas, that\u2019s basically what they do. They don\u2019t leave the Scion with nothing, they leave nothing of the Scion at all as the Scion becomes part of the original god.</div> </div> </div> </div>The nature of Deva Divinity is such that they were never <i>not</i> the original God in the first place, whether they knew it or not. Also, Deva Avatars don't disappear, never to be seen again absorbed into the Borg <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They still exist, having realized their Unity with their overselves, and often pop out in various stories <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 06-01-2020, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:11:00-07:00","id":1393431,"title":"","content":"Yeah I don\u2019t think many people would love to spend months of playing a game, maybe even years and then have it all turn out to be a waste of time.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also like why would they even do it to begin with? They\u2019re already a god anyways so why would they want to steal someone else\u2019? They\u2019ve already made and have their own mantles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","user":"Magicjohnny","date":". 06-01-2020, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:12:39-07:00","id":1393432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393128-on-mantles-what-the-heck?p=1393428#post1393428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There really aren't any Gods that assholish in the core books, or mostly in general... despite what DnD et all like to throw about, 'Evil' Gods aren't really a thing, and that idea is slipping into 1e Aztec territory, and while you can do that in your games, it's going counter to the respectful tone 2e has generally been trying to set.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair enough. I would be happy with a non-god, like a Titan. Although that wouldn't exactly be them taking a mantle, but it would feel close to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:15:33-07:00","id":1393433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393128-on-mantles-what-the-heck?p=1393431#post1393431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I don\u2019t think many people would love to spend months of playing a game, maybe even years and then have it all turn out to be a waste of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Neall has said there's going to be a failure state to Demi-God where you don't actually succeed at becoming a god. So, this would just be another way to fail, not the only way to fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T09:27:43-07:00","id":1393456,"title":"","content":"All the possible outcome of apotheosis, god subsuming the scion, scion subsuming the god, scion becoming a new god altogether.<br /> All of those options is something that shouldve already been discussed between the player and the Storyguide.<br /> <br /> But i will say that being subsumed into the god isnt an unappealing option if you intended to play as Thor from the very beginning. <br /> <br /> You just started as an incarnation or another type of scion of thor at Origin, Hero and Demigod and upon advancing at God you continue playing, just as Thor + the new things you accomplished prior to apotheosis.<br /> <br /> All that said, and i hope this is well addressed in the God book, apotheosis in most pantheon is an incredibly traumatic event identity wise.<br /> Again this is relative from one pantheon to another but all in all, id be surprised for anyones sense of self to remain unscated after losing your mortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 06-01-2020, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:01:40-07:00","id":1393511,"title":"","content":"I think playing with god will not be as easy as it seams. Fate will be a big pain in the game for sure, as the gods are locked in their conditions. Avatars (as temporary projections of the gods in lower tiers) will have more freedom, but still with several blocks.<br /> <br /> The description of Columbia give some idea of what happens when she is distorted to fit the views of the believers, and I think it will be better described, starting from Demigod. The Virtues and Fatebinding will start pulling the game more and more as legend rise, to the point the worst enemy of the god will be his own legend and fate (Ragnarok and all the prophecies of Delphi are exemples).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T04:36:47-07:00","id":1394753,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it seems like your mantle is directly associated with your divine identity.<br /> <br /> Which makes sense as to why more powerful (Legendary) characters are able to have several mantles at once. As it fits in with the theme of <i>&quot;I have many names&quot;</i> that is often associated with old and powerful entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}